class.description:
A [ResourceSaveResult] is returned by [method ResourceSaver.save_result]. Unlike [method ResourceSaver.save], which returns only an [enum Error] code, it also holds the message the saver printed, so the caller can show or log [i]why[/i] a save failed. It is read-only after creation.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var result := ResourceSaver.save_result(save_game, "user://save_1.tres")
if not result.ok:
	push_error("Saving failed: %s" % result.error_message)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
ResourceSaveResult result = ResourceSaver.SaveResult(saveGame, "user://save_1.tres");
if (!result.Ok)
{
    GD.PushError($"Saving failed: {result.ErrorMessage}");
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
In C#, [code]ResourceSaver.TrySave(resource, path, out Error error)[/code] offers the usual [code]Try[/code] pattern.
